  "investigation_notes": "Uploads failing due to filesystem permissions on upload directory \u2014 not database, not disk full.\n\n**Evidence:**\n- `incidentlab-app-1` `running` Up 5s, `incidentlab-db-1` `running` Up 11s `(healthy)` (E1). App mount `/srv/lab-data` -> `/data` `rw:true`, user `1000:1000` (E4). DB `healthy`, `running:true` (E7).\n- App `/health` `503 {\"status\":\"unhealthy\"}` (E2).\n- DB logs: `database system is ready to accept connections` (E6), with `pg_isready` `health_status: healthy` restarts (E3). Rules out DB dependency as cause.\n- App logs show successful `POST /upload 200 OK` then `POST /upload 500 Internal Server Error` with `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/tmp/69bf62c95c93ac02542580393a4111e3.part' -> '/data/uploads/69bf62c95c93ac02542580393a4111e3'` in `os.replace(tmp_path, final_path)` at `/app/main.py line 63` (E5).\n- Health-check failure is same cause: `health check failed` + `PermissionError: [Errno 13] Permission denied: '/data/uploads/.health-078c39cd15a0037e'` in `open(probe,\"wb\")` at `/app/main.py line 116` leading to `GET /health 503` (E5). So `503` (E2) is symptom, not root cause.\n- Host path `/srv/lab-data/uploads`: `is_dir:true`, `owner_uid:1000 owner_gid:1000`, `mode:0555`, `app_uid:1000 app_gid:1000`, `app_user_can_write:false` (E8).\n- Parent `/srv/lab-data`: `owner 1000:1000`, `mode:0755`, `app_user_can_write:true` (E9) \u2014 parent writable, problem isolated to `uploads/`.\n- Mount is `rw:true` (E4), so not read-only mount \u2014 denied by mode bits.\n- Filesystem for `/srv/lab-data`: `use_percent:9.0`, `available_mb:410.6`, `inode_use_percent:0.2` (E10) \u2014 rules out capacity / inode exhaustion.\n\n**Conclusion:** Root cause is permission bits `0555` on bind-mounted `/srv/lab-data/uploads` preventing UID `1000` write, causing `PermissionError` on upload final move and health probe.",
